drm: sunxi: edp: bring the link back after a replug or a failed training

Unplugging stops the main link, plugging back in only rereads the dpcd and
edid. When the display pipe stayed active (a console, no compositor), no one
asks for a modeset and the link is never trained again, so the screen stays
black until a program changes the mode. Link training can also fail on a sink
that isn't ready yet: a typec dock with a dp-to-hdmi converter fails hbr2
inter-lane alignment if trained right after hpd, and works a second later.

From the hpd thread, commit a full modeset on the active pipe (which retrains
the link) 1s after a plugin, and 2s after an enable that failed, at most 5
times per plug event. A successful enable clears the request, so nothing
extra happens when a compositor already set the mode after the hotplug event,
and a pipe that is off is left alone: whoever turns it on trains the link.

Upstream-Status: Pending

